/*
 * Copyright 2026 Alp Lab AB
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * MDIO-managed-PHY compile-only variant of the aen-ethernet-link bring-up.
 * Applied ON TOP of the board's default fixed-link overlay
 * (boards/alp_e1m_aen801_m55_he_ae822fa0e5597ls0_rtss_he.overlay, which
 * already routes the MDC/MDIO pins in pinctrl_eth): enables the `mdio`
 * controller + `eth_phy_managed` TI DP83825 child added to
 * zephyr/dts/alif/ensemble_e8_peripherals.dtsi, and repoints &ethernet's
 * phy-handle at it instead of the default fixed-link eth_phy.
 *
 * COMPILE-PROOF in CI (see the mdio-managed test entry in testcase.yaml):
 * closes that the mdio_dwmac_alif driver binds, phy_ti_dp83825 binds on the
 * bus, and the upstream eth_dwmac core's phy_link path compiles with a
 * managed PHY.
 *
 * The MDIO layer itself HAS since been exercised on real E8 silicon by a
 * Flow C ITCM RAM-run of this variant (#1244):
 *
 *   [eth] MDIO PHY@0 id=2000a140 (DP83825=2000a140)
 *   [eth] PHY regs: ANAR=01e1 ANLPAR=0000 PHYSTS=0002 RCSR=00e1
 *
 * That run reported `PHY link DOWN (BMSR=7849)` -- no cable on that desk --
 * so link/traffic over the managed path is still unproven; reading the PHY
 * ID needs no link, which is what made the address answerable without one.
 *
 * This overlay deliberately does NOT override `reg`: it inherits the PHY
 * address from `eth_phy_managed` in
 * zephyr/dts/alif/ensemble_e8_peripherals.dtsi, so there is ONE source of
 * truth for it. Keep it that way -- the fix for the wrong address (1 -> 0)
 * belongs at that node, not here.
 */

&mdio {
	status = "okay";
};

&eth_phy_managed {
	status = "okay";
};

&ethernet {
	phy-handle = <&eth_phy_managed>;
};
